.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.CONTEXTUSAGE" "3JS" "August 14, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.contextUsage \- LanguageModel: contextUsage property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]contextUsage\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] interface returns the number of context window
tokens currently consumed by the session that calls it, including
initial prompts and all subsequent turns.
.PP
This value increases every time you call \f[CR]prompt()\f[R],
\f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R], or \f[CR]append()\f[R].
.PP
Compare \f[CR]contextUsage\f[R] with
\f[CR]LanguageModel.contextWindow\f[R] to determine how many tokens
remain.
When \f[CR]contextUsage\f[R] would exceed \f[CR]contextWindow\f[R],
subsequent method calls throw a \f[CR]QuotaExceededError\f[R] and the
\f[CR]contextoverflow\f[R] event fires.
.PP
To estimate how many tokens a new prompt would use before sending it,
call \f[CR]LanguageModel.measureContextUsage()\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A number representing the current context window usage in tokens.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Monitoring context usage during a conversation
This example writes context usage to the console after a session prompt
completes.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();

\f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt(\(dqTell me about the history of the internet.\(dq);

console.log(
  \(gaContext used: ${session.contextUsage} / ${session.contextWindow} tokens\(ga,
);
.EE
.SS Warning when the context is nearly full
The following example uses a function to verify that context is
available before calling \f[CR]LanguageModel.prompt()\f[R].
It first calculates the remaining context and passes that value to
\f[CR]measureContextUsage()\f[R].
If \f[CR]needed\f[R] is less than or equal to \f[CR]remaining\f[R], it
returns \f[CR]true\f[R] and the session continues.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] promptText = \(dqLet me ask you an interesting question...\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] contextAvailable(promptText) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] remaining = session.contextWindow \- session.contextUsage;
  \f[B]const\f[R] needed = \f[B]await\f[R] session.measureContextUsage(promptText);

  \f[B]return\f[R] needed <= remaining;
}

\f[B]if\f[R] (\f[B]await\f[R] contextAvailable(promptText)) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] response = \f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt(promptText);
  console.log(response);
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  console.warn(\(dqPrompt skipped: Not enough context window remaining.\(dq);
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
